# Purpose

This document defines the motion and animation standards that establish a responsive, predictable, and consistent interaction language across the hubIO platform.

Its purpose is to ensure that motion communicates change, supports usability, and improves perceived performance while remaining aligned with the Engineering Constitution.

---

# Scope

This standard defines:

* Motion philosophy
* Motion principles
* Motion language
* Animation hierarchy
* Motion timing
* Motion performance
* Motion accessibility
* Motion governance

It intentionally excludes component-specific animation behavior and implementation details, which are defined by their respective Engineering Standards.

---

# Constitutional Interpretation

This document extends the hubIO Engineering Constitution.

It applies constitutional engineering principles to motion design, ensuring every animation improves usability, reinforces clarity, and remains consistent throughout the product.

